Public response:

The structural signs can only be identified if C actually varies in the experiment that is run.

C is defined as nectar caffeine concentration.  Citrus × sinensis, sweet orange, does not make caffeine in its nectar or tissues in the wild. A caffeine knock-out in orange is a knock-out of essentially zero.  In the stated experimental system Var(C)≈0 over the whole experiment, so the three C-originating structural coefficients a, c and e, and the mediated effects a·b and c·d, are not identified from a caffeine knock-out in oranges. The model is not testable in a non-caffeine system.

That is the formal answer J: Impossible to tell from the given statement.

Remark on biological plausibility if the model is taken as a hypothetical caffeine-producing system.  In the coffee / bumble-bee literature nectar caffeine is a CNS stimulant / memory enhancer.  The most parsimonious reading is

* C → F  a < 0 : higher C increases arousal/learning speed and shortens mean flower-level handling/foraging duration per visit;
* F → Y  b < 0 : on a time-budgeted forager longer per-flower residence trades off against flowers visited per bout, so longer F is associated with lower pollination throughput and lower yield;
* C → R  c > 0 : caffeine increases flower/patch constancy and return probability, pollinator retention R increases with C;
* R → Y  d > 0 : greater retention means more repeat visits and more effective pollination;
* C → Y direct e < 0 : synthesis/sequestration of caffeine is a metabolic/resource cost to the plant net of pollinator mediation.

Hence a·b >0 and c·d >0, the two pollinator mediated indirect effects are yield positive and dominate the direct metabolic cost e<0, giving the overall net positive effect of nectar caffeine on yield that is lost on knock-out. That is the sign pattern a -, b -, c +, d +, e -, choice B, the nuanced cost-trade-off version of the textbook all-positive A. The all-positive A is the naïve textbook simplification; D/G variants reflect alternative handling/retention trade-off readings.

For oranges as stated, however, the biological impossibility of C makes the sign pattern formally unidentified.

